ERROR HANDLING


    - Types of errors
        * Syntax Errors (Compile time errors)
            indentation, wrong syntax
        * Runtime Errors
            ZeroDivisionError, indexerror
        * Logical Errors
            wrong logic

    - Runtime errors can be handled using error handling
        
        * try
        * except
        * finally

        * raise
        * assert

        keywords
            * block & key


    - Try & Except
        * try block contains codes that may or may not work.
        * except block contain codes on how to handle any error raised by the try block.
    - Try & Finally
        * finally blocks executes aside of errors in try block

    
    
    
    - Raise
        * manually raise an error
    - Assert
        * automatically raises an error